  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Photographic Volume",
    "overview": "The portfolio presents travel and wildlife photographs as authored collections with the gravitas of coffee-table books. Warm paper and dark brown ink frame the public index; a dark exhibition wall holds the complete photographic galleries. Large, expressive serif titles establish authorship while quiet sans-serif copy and monospaced navigation support reading.\n\nThe photobook shelf extends this inherited identity with cloth bindings, photographic cover plates, page edges, warm wood, and individual paper spreads. This tactile vocabulary belongs to books and their inspection cards; it does not require every interface surface to become three-dimensional. The hero and galleries retain their existing visual roles.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Photography keeps its complete composition, with room around the image.",
      "Oversized serif titles sit beside restrained utility text.",
      "Paper, cloth, mats, and wood provide material depth.",
      "Each collection has a distinct binding within one coherent library.",
